*> Implementation test of the name index of formats/src/zip.cob (ZIP-FIND; 22 §8.4 last paragraph: a
*> hash or sorted index of the names, built once per pack, instead of a scan): an archive of 10,000
*> entries (made here: stored entries without data, one central directory) answers 10,000 lookups of
*> present names and 10,000 of absent names in well under the time a scan needs, every lookup gives the
*> right entry, the first of two entries with one name wins, names of 1 and 256 bytes are found,
*> prefixes, other cases and other lengths of a name are absent. A scan of this archive takes about two
*> seconds (2.1 s measured before the index existed); the bound below is half a second.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ZIP-INDEX.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY FORMATS.
 01 WS-LOCAL-HEADER.
    05 LH-SIGNATURE        PIC X(4) VALUE X"504B0304".
    05 LH-VERSION          BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 20.
    05 LH-FLAGS            BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-METHOD           BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-TIME             BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-DATE             BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-CRC              BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-COMPRESSED       BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-SIZE             BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 LH-NAME-LENGTH      BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED.
    05 LH-EXTRA-LENGTH     BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CENTRAL-HEADER.
    05 CH-SIGNATURE        PIC X(4) VALUE X"504B0102".
    05 CH-VERSION-MADE     BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 20.
    05 CH-VERSION          BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 20.
    05 CH-FLAGS            BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-METHOD           BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-TIME             BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-DATE             BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-CRC              BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-COMPRESSED       BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-SIZE             BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-NAME-LENGTH      BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED.
    05 CH-EXTRA-LENGTH     BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-COMMENT-LENGTH   BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-DISK             BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-INTERNAL         BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-EXTERNAL         BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 CH-LOCAL            BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-END-RECORD.
    05 ER-SIGNATURE        PIC X(4) VALUE X"504B0506".
    05 ER-DISK             BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 ER-CD-DISK          BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
    05 ER-ENTRIES-HERE     BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED.
    05 ER-ENTRIES          BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED.
    05 ER-CD-SIZE          BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
    05 ER-CD-OFFSET        BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
    05 ER-COMMENT-LENGTH   BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ARCHIVE             PIC X(1400000).
 01 WS-CENTRAL             PIC X(800000).
 01 WS-LOCAL-USED          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CENTRAL-USED        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TOTAL-LENGTH        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENTRY-NAME          PIC X(256).
 01 WS-ENTRY-LENGTH        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NUMBER              PIC 9(5).
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-PATH-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZIP                 USAGE POINTER.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INDEX               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WRONG               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SHOWN               PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-ACCESS              PIC X COMP-X VALUE 2.
 01 WS-DENY                PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-DEVICE              PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-HANDLE              PIC X(4).
 01 WS-OFFSET              PIC X(8) COMP-X.
 01 WS-BYTES               PIC X(4) COMP-X.
 01 WS-FLAGS               PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-DIRECTORY           PIC X(64).
 01 WS-CLOCK.
    05 FILLER              PIC X(8).
    05 WS-HH               PIC 99.
    05 WS-MM               PIC 99.
    05 WS-SS               PIC 99.
    05 WS-CC               PIC 99.
    05 FILLER              PIC X(5).
 01 WS-START-CS            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NOW-CS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ELAPSED             BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
*>   The archive: 9996 regular names, "a", a 256-byte name, and "dup.txt" twice (entries 9999 and 10000).
     MOVE 1 TO WS-LOCAL-USED WS-CENTRAL-USED
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 10000
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENTRY-NAME
         EVALUATE TRUE
             WHEN WS-I <= 9996
                 MOVE WS-I TO WS-NUMBER
                 STRING "dir/entry-" WS-NUMBER ".txt" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-ENTRY-NAME
                 MOVE 19 TO WS-ENTRY-LENGTH
             WHEN WS-I = 9997
                 MOVE "a" TO WS-ENTRY-NAME
                 MOVE 1 TO WS-ENTRY-LENGTH
             WHEN WS-I = 9998
                 MOVE ALL "n" TO WS-ENTRY-NAME
                 MOVE ".txt" TO WS-ENTRY-NAME(253:4)
                 MOVE 256 TO WS-ENTRY-LENGTH
             WHEN OTHER
                 MOVE "dup.txt" TO WS-ENTRY-NAME
                 MOVE 7 TO WS-ENTRY-LENGTH
         END-EVALUATE
         MOVE WS-ENTRY-LENGTH TO LH-NAME-LENGTH CH-NAME-LENGTH
         COMPUTE CH-LOCAL = WS-LOCAL-USED - 1
         MOVE WS-LOCAL-HEADER TO WS-ARCHIVE(WS-LOCAL-USED:30)
         MOVE WS-ENTRY-NAME(1:WS-ENTRY-LENGTH) TO WS-ARCHIVE(WS-LOCAL-USED + 30:WS-ENTRY-LENGTH)
         ADD 30 TO WS-LOCAL-USED
         ADD WS-ENTRY-LENGTH TO WS-LOCAL-USED
         MOVE WS-CENTRAL-HEADER TO WS-CENTRAL(WS-CENTRAL-USED:46)
         MOVE WS-ENTRY-NAME(1:WS-ENTRY-LENGTH) TO WS-CENTRAL(WS-CENTRAL-USED + 46:WS-ENTRY-LENGTH)
         ADD 46 TO WS-CENTRAL-USED
         ADD WS-ENTRY-LENGTH TO WS-CENTRAL-USED
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 10000 TO ER-ENTRIES-HERE ER-ENTRIES
     COMPUTE ER-CD-SIZE = WS-CENTRAL-USED - 1
     COMPUTE ER-CD-OFFSET = WS-LOCAL-USED - 1
     MOVE WS-CENTRAL(1:WS-CENTRAL-USED - 1) TO WS-ARCHIVE(WS-LOCAL-USED:WS-CENTRAL-USED - 1)
     COMPUTE WS-TOTAL-LENGTH = WS-LOCAL-USED + WS-CENTRAL-USED - 2
     MOVE WS-END-RECORD TO WS-ARCHIVE(WS-TOTAL-LENGTH + 1:22)
     ADD 22 TO WS-TOTAL-LENGTH
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "zip index the header records are 30, 46 and 22 bytes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 98 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = FUNCTION LENGTH(WS-LOCAL-HEADER) + FUNCTION LENGTH(WS-CENTRAL-HEADER)
         + FUNCTION LENGTH(WS-END-RECORD)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Write it under build/formats-test.
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-DIRECTORY
     MOVE "build/formats-test" TO WS-DIRECTORY
     CALL "CBL_CREATE_DIR" USING WS-DIRECTORY
     MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "build/formats-test/index-10000.zip" TO WS-PATH
     CALL "CBL_CREATE_FILE" USING WS-PATH WS-ACCESS WS-DENY WS-DEVICE WS-HANDLE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OFFSET
     MOVE WS-TOTAL-LENGTH TO WS-BYTES
     CALL "CBL_WRITE_FILE" USING WS-HANDLE WS-OFFSET WS-BYTES WS-FLAGS WS-ARCHIVE
     CALL "CBL_CLOSE_FILE" USING WS-HANDLE
     MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
     MOVE 34 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH

     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-COUNT" USING WS-ZIP WS-COUNT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "zip index the 10,000-entry archive opens with 10000 entries" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 10000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING "0 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     IF WS-STATUS NOT = 0
         MOVE "open failed" TO TL-OBSERVED
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   10,000 lookups of present names and 10,000 of absent names, timed.
     MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CLOCK
     COMPUTE WS-START-CS = WS-HH * 360000 + WS-MM * 6000 + WS-SS * 100 + WS-CC
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WRONG
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 9996
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-NAME
         MOVE WS-I TO WS-NUMBER
         STRING "dir/entry-" WS-NUMBER ".txt" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-NAME
         MOVE 19 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
         CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
         IF WS-INDEX NOT = WS-I
             ADD 1 TO WS-WRONG
         END-IF
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-NAME
         STRING "dir/other-" WS-NUMBER ".txt" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-NAME
         CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
         IF WS-INDEX NOT = 0
             ADD 1 TO WS-WRONG
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CLOCK
     COMPUTE WS-NOW-CS = WS-HH * 360000 + WS-MM * 6000 + WS-SS * 100 + WS-CC
     COMPUTE WS-ELAPSED = WS-NOW-CS - WS-START-CS
     IF WS-ELAPSED < 0
         ADD 8640000 TO WS-ELAPSED
     END-IF
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "zip index 9996 present and 9996 absent names are all answered correctly" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-WRONG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "zip index the lookups take under half a second (no scan of the 10,000 names)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-ELAPSED < 50
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE WS-ELAPSED TO WS-SHOWN
     DISPLAY "zip index lookups of 19992 names took " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " centiseconds"

*>   Odd names.
     MOVE "a" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index a name of 1 byte is entry 9997" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 9997 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE ALL "n" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE ".txt" TO WS-NAME(253:4)
     MOVE 256 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index a name of 256 bytes is entry 9998" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 9998 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "dup.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 7 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index of two entries named dup.txt the first is found (9999)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 9999 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "dir/entry-0000" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 14 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index a prefix of a name is absent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "DIR/ENTRY-00007.TXT" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 19 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index names are case sensitive" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "dir/entry-00007.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 0 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index a name of length 0 is absent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 257 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index a name of length 257 is absent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 7 TO WS-INDEX
     MOVE "dir/entry-00007.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 18 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE "zip index the same name one byte short is absent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-INDEX TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ZIP-INDEX.
